  "notes": "くるくる is a mimetic word ({擬態語|ぎたいご}) describing light, continuous spinning or circular motion. Also describes tight curls.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- くるくる{回|まわ}る: to spin round and round\n- くるくる{巻|ま}く: to roll up tightly\n- くるくるの{髪|かみ}: curly hair\n- くるくるパーマ: tight perm\n\nUSAGE:\nCan function as an adverb (くるくる{回|まわ}る), a noun modifier (くるくるの{髪|かみ}), or with と (くるくると{舞|ま}う). Implies light, quick, pleasant rotation.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ぐるぐる: spinning (heavier, often implies dizziness or being wrapped tightly)\n- くるりと: a single spin or turn (one rotation)\n- くるくる: continuous, light spinning (multiple rotations)",
